From 891abe093be181b1a766efca586f33eb8a727457 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:05:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): standalone Pause and Home entries in the operation
 list

A Pause / Home / Optional-stop entry is its own entity kind
(schema::ProgramEntry + OperationMeta position), not an Operation, so
setup::operation_order and every walk on it (post tool/freshness gate,
rest ahead, program sim, setup sheet, tool list, verify) never see one.
program_entry::sequence orders ops and entries for the list;
posting folds each entry into the PARAM AfterOperation word of the
posted op before it (the per-op #110 word, byte-identical), honouring
Suppress and "Skip pauses and homes"; an entry before every posted op,
or a stop and a home in one gap, refuse the post by name.

Commands: AddProgramEntry, EditProgramEntry (action / suppressed);
ReorderOperation, DeleteEntity, CreateOperation's append and
DeleteSetup's refusal count positions over the sequence. Project file:
an `entry` entity kind with an `entry` payload, no version rung (older
readers refuse the unknown kind by name). UI: add rows in every
operation-list menu, an entry row with its own menu, entries drag like
ops.

Fixes #155

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
